  "text": "H1 selects the shortest estimated job-completion horizon; H9 favors remaining work while strongly favoring faster machines and penalizing waiting. I combine the parents’ best-action-gap and relative-variability triggers: choose H1 when either indicates differentiated action costs, otherwise choose H9. These cost signals are a selection hypothesis, not evidence that either H wins on a given state.\n\n```python\ndef use_heuristics(state):\n    gap = 0.0\n    if state[\"availability\"][\"action_delta_best_gap\"]:\n        gap = state[\"action_delta_best_gap\"]\n    if gap > 0.05:\n        return 1\n    if state[\"availability\"][\"action_delta_mean\"]:\n        if state[\"availability\"][\"action_delta_std\"]:\n            if state[\"action_delta_std\"] > state[\"action_delta_mean\"]:\n                return 1\n    return 9\n```",
